  "limitations": [
    "Original medium-fi exterior starts with cleared public-domain Qualla photographs and original public-domain HABS PA-5346/PA-5346-A site, floor, elevation and section drawings. Main-house occupied rooms, open terraces, floor heights and east-west stream stair replace earlier generalized assumptions. Raster tracing, core partitions and geographic registration remain interpreted; current review is pending in qa.json. Old copied plan and miniature images are excluded.",
    "Crossing terrace axes, stone core, red glazing, hanging stair and clear underside are modeled. Exact room plans, hidden facades, guest-wing openings, structural repairs and roof drains are simplified interpretations.",
    "The short static stream, cascade and rock ledges illustrate the house-waterfall relationship. They are not a hydrologic simulation, exact geological reconstruction or current water-level claim. Surrounding terrain is preserved rather than flattened.",
    "The north upper-floor bridge and curved exterior stair are distinct from the first-floor entrance. Guest floor +10.3314 m is an interpreted threshold above independent ground, not a combined-site floor survey. Original HABS floor/site topology and relative levels control the geometry; manually traced plan proportions are not georeferenced CAD. Source-interpolated ground under buildings and actual excavation remain under review.",
    "No interior furnishings, sculpture replica, surrounding forest or external image textures are included. Local reference photography remains outside runtime packs."
  ],
